-- 0164 - Two KPI metric keys, `quotes-sent` and `sales-cycle-days` (ADR 0144), and one bell
-- kind, `kpi-digest` (ADR 0145). Seven metric lists widen: kpi_target, kpi_allocation_line,
-- kpi_allocation_share, kpi_assignment_line, kpi_month_value, kpi_role_metric, kpi_alert_sent
-- (fourteen keys plus two: sixteen). Both bell kind lists widen (0150's sixty-six plus one:
-- sixty-seven). `notification_subject_kind_known` is untouched: the digest points at the
-- existing `kpi-scorecard`, `kpi-target`, `kpi-allocation` and `kpi-team`. Lists copied by hand.
--
-- Additive: each list is widened by DROP + ADD, so every row 0150 and earlier accepted
-- still passes. ORDER: migrate BEFORE deploy; the old build never emits the new values.
-- Re-runnable: DROP ... IF EXISTS before every ADD. Hand-written for 0047's reason.
-- Each ADD scans its table under a lock: give up after 10 s instead of queueing writers.
SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '10s';--> statement-breakpoint

